        {
          "id": "PRR_kwDOOSVefs8AAAABIBEaew",
          "commit": {
            "abbreviatedOid": "28fb133"
          },
          "author": "dghgit",
          "authorAssociation": "COLLABORATOR",
          "state": "COMMENTED",
          "body": "",
          "createdAt": "2026-08-01T00:12:37Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-08-01T00:12:37Z",
          "comments": [
            {
              "originalPosition": 32,
              "body": "I think the other thing is we're really trying to concentrate on encoding with this document - if we start getting into all the features of ASN.1 the language, we'll wind up just writing another copy of the standard (and we already know how that story ends!) I would just leave it as \"Advanced features...\" otherwise all it will take is someone to write \"RFC  <some-suitably-demonic-number>: Insane things I found I could do with ASN.1 while reading in the bathtub\" and we, or someone after us, will also find themselves rewriting the standard. The point is to get people far enough that they're not intimidated by having to use ASN.1 encodings, after that they should be able work things out for themselves. At the moment it seems most people can't even get off the starting block.",
              "createdAt": "2026-08-01T00:12:37Z",
              "updatedAt": "2026-08-01T00:12:37Z"
            }
          ]
        },
